{"dossier_job_key":"dossier:2023-luna-next4-v2:2023:VNM:19640","iso3":"VNM","ruler_name":"Nguyễn Phú Trọng","score":5.5,"range":{"lower":4.5,"upper":6.5},"confidence":61.0,"rationale":"Trọng’s record supports 5.5: durable health and welfare institutions and explicit social priorities, but limited evidence of attributable 2023 gains. Vietnam’s national plan made health insurance, poverty reduction, welfare, human-resource development, and living standards central objectives. The country maintained a nationwide primary-health-care system and entered 2023 with large long-run poverty and human-development gains. Yet post-COVID recovery was uneven: manufacturing workers lost hours or jobs, informal work expanded, and stronger safety nets were still needed. Rural, educational, gender, water, and sanitation gaps persisted, and many households remained vulnerable to health, climate, and labor shocks. Most favorable evidence concerns inherited systems, official plans, or long-run outcomes produced by several administrations and provincial delivery. Trọng had strong strategic Party authority, but collective leadership and ministries mediated implementation. These durable institutions and real policy priorities exceed a failing 4; incomplete delivery, inequality, and weak ruler-specific outcome evidence prevent the clear baseline-adjusted gains required for 6–7.","lower":"Nationwide primary health, explicit welfare priorities, and substantial long-run gains make a predominantly failing 4 too harsh.","higher":"Official plans and inherited systems do not establish clear attributable 2023 gains or equitable quality.","pos":["E024","E025","E023"],"neg":["E021","E020"],"contrary":["E021","E020"],"baseline":"Trọng inherited decades of development gains alongside rural and gender gaps; post-COVID recovery, global demand, provinces, and collective leadership constrained attribution.","attribution":"Trọng exercised high strategic Party authority, while collective bodies, ministries, provinces, donors, and long policy lags shared responsibility.","source_mix":"Official planning, WHO, World Bank, UNDP, and institutional reports; implementation evidence is limited and official-heavy."}
